      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/man-la-yahduruhu-al-faqih:4:20:3",
      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/20/5177",
      "text": [
        ": \"إِنَّ أَمِيرَ اَلْمُؤْمِنِينَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ سُئِلَ عَنْ رَجُلٍ كَانَ جَالِساً مَعَ قَوْمٍ فَمَاتَ وَ هُوَ مَعَهُمْ أَوْ رَجُلٍ وُجِدَ فِي قَبِيلَةٍ أَوْ عَلَى دَارِ قَوْمٍ فَادُّعِيَ عَلَيْهِمْ قَالَ \"لَيْسَ عَلَيْهِمْ قَوَدٌ وَ لاَ يُطَلُّ دَمُهُ عَلَيْهِمُ اَلدِّيَةُ\" \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5177 - Muhammad ibn Sahl narrated from his father, from some of his elders, from Abu Abdullah Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as), who said:\n\"The Commander of the Faithful (as) was asked about a man who was sitting with a group of people and died while among them, or a man who was found dead in a tribe or near the house of some people, and they were accused of his death.\nImam (as) said: 'There is no retaliation (qisas) upon them, nor is his blood wasted. However, the blood money (diyyah) is upon them.'\""
        ]
      }
    },
